2026-10-31 04:13 Code findings while checking (not fixed, not in scope):
1. OCP::Config::validate has no caller in lib/ or bin/ -- only t/ runs it. ocp apply never reports a config error up front: network.* (lb_pool, l2, pod_cidr overlaps), cilium:, gpu.amd:, robocop.security_level, control_planes[].node_ip. Code that relies on it: Bootstrap.pm cp_node_ip ('OCP::Config has refused a malformed one already'), Config.pm comment ('so ocp apply lists it with every other config error'). The skill's node_ip paragraph ('refused before anything is ordered') and the gpu.amd 'validate error' line therefore hold only once validate is wired in; state lane.
2. LB-IPAM failure (e.g. multi-node without network.lb_pool) prints '[WARN] LB-IPAM setup failed' on STDOUT, deploy path (Apply/Deploy.pm) and reconcile path (Apply/Drift.pm), and is not counted as a failed component -- unlike the Cilium Gateway (STDERR + counted, k231). Against the STDOUT/STDERR rule and ADR 0017.
3. _validate_network reports no unknown key under network:, lb_pool, l2 (a typo like network.lbpool is silently ignored), unlike cilium: and gpu.amd:. Also no start<=stop check on lb_pool.
4. DeployImage.pm _resolve_cluster: die "--cluster '$self->cluster' contradicts ..." interpolates the object (OCP::Cmd::DeployImage=HASH(...)->cluster), not the value. Its POD also says --cluster 'must match the spec name' / 'dies on a mismatching --cluster'; the code only compares --cluster with OCP_CLUSTER, and the name selects nothing (only printed).
5. Node/Ls.pm POD says pool is read only from annotation ocp.internal/pool; the code falls back to ocp.yaml's pools (_pools_of). Nothing in lib/ sets that annotation.
6. Node/TrustHost.pm comment says 'a closed or non-terminal stdin answers no'; the code reads one line, so a piped 'y' confirms (only EOF/other answers no). Comment only.

